## Servo_Arduino

This library allows an Arduino board to control RC (hobby) servo motors.

This library is capable of managing a large number of servo motors efficiently. It optimizes the use of hardware timers, enabling control of up to 12 servos with a single timer.

**Supported Architecture controller:**

- avr
- megaavr

For more information about this library please visit:[Arduino Servo Library](https://www.arduino.cc/reference/en/libraries/servo/)

**Servo_Arduino Library Information:**
name=Servo
version=1.2.2
author=Michael Margolis, Arduino
maintainer=Arduino <info@arduino.cc>
category=Device Control
url= [Arduino Library](https://www.arduino.cc/reference/en/libraries/servo/)

***

## SPI_Arduino

This library allows you to communicate with SPI devices, with the Arduino board as the controller device. SPI is a synchronous serial data protocol used by microcontrollers for communicating with one or more peripheral devices quickly over short distances. It uses three lines common to all devices (MISO, MOSI and SCK) and one specific for each device.

**Supported Architecture controller:**

- avr
- megaavr

For more information about this library please visit:[Arduino SPI Library](https://docs.arduino.cc/learn/communication/spi/)

**Servo_Arduino Library Information:**
name=SPI
version=1.0
author= Arduino
maintainer=Arduino <info@arduino.cc>
category= Communication
url= [Arduino Library](https://www.arduino.cc/reference/en/libraries/servo/)

